<title>SWITZERLAND: SWISS BOND MARKET CLOSING REPORT.</title>
<headline>SWISS BOND MARKET CLOSING REPORT.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss bonds ended firmer, moving higher as German debt prices rose after the Bundesbank said it was setting an unchanged fixed, three-percent rate on its latest securities repurchase tender.</p>
<p>Some market participants had believed the Bundesbank would set a variable rate tender, speculating that such a move would allow German money rates to rise to offset weakness in the German mark.</p>
<p>Swiss trade was generally quiet. Shorter Swiss maturities were also firmer, including LIFFE's EuroSwiss contract.  </p>
<p>-- Tuesday's closing prices as follows:</p>
<p>Conf futures up 15 at 120.22.</p>
<p>Comi medium-term bond up 15 at 113.15</p>
<p>Euro Swiss francs up two at 98.45.</p>
<p>4-1/2 Jun 2007 bond 108.55/65 yield 3.445 pct</p>
<p>(Monday 108.45/55 yield 3.457 pct)</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
